    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7961" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cĭcātrīcōsus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of scars</i>, <i>covered with scars</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tergum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Am. 1, 1, 290</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">facies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 4, 1, 61</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ira (personified),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ira, 2, 35, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col. Arb. 11, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">putatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 27, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of a writing, <i>amended</i> or <i>polished</i> here and there, <i><span class="en">Quint. 10,
				4, 3</span></i>; v. the context.</div>
